## Summary

Implemented mrr-incremental-fetch-3sl.5: TUI selection is now keyed by `domain.MRKey{ProjectID, IID}` instead of column+row position.

**Key changes:**
- `boardWidget.SetMRs(mrs, selected) domain.MRKey` (internal/tui/board.go) owns focus resolution: it finds the selected MR anywhere on the board (fixing the old `TryRestoreFocus`'s same-IID-different-project collision), follows it across columns on a phase change, and falls back to the same row (clamped) or the first non-empty column when the MR is gone.
- `Model.selected` replaces `prevFocusMR`; `applyMRFilter()`'s one-line `m.selected = m.board.SetMRs(displayMRs, m.selected)` fixes all 8 former call sites by construction, per the ADR.
- Added `domain.MergeRequest.Key()` helper; deleted `TryRestoreFocus`.

**Verification:**
- New tests: `internal/tui/board_test.go` (collision, cross-column follow, both fallback cases) and 4 selection-identity tests in `model_test.go` (sort, sprint toggle, view toggle, fetch swap).
- `just check` passes clean.
- agent-tui live gate against gl.nsesi.io confirmed selection survives sort and a view-toggle round trip. Note: screenshots in this sandbox carry no color info, so I verified focus via the detail panel's text (IID/title) rather than the highlight color — documented in progress.md.

Bead closed, tracker synced, decision and session summary saved to engram.
